node_modules/
dist/
.DS_Store
*.local
*.pdf

# Patch/merge backups. `patch` and `git` drop these next to the file they came
# from, so a `git add -A` while one exists commits a byte-for-byte duplicate of
# a source file under a name nothing imports — silent, and easy to miss in a
# large diff. Observed during the C4 review, when a prototype patch left
# src/pdf/layout.js.orig behind.
*.orig
*.rej

# AI assistant session data — never commit (may contain full transcripts)
.claude/
lib/
coverage/

# research/ is deliberately SPLIT, not ignored wholesale.
#
# The active engineering record IS committed: the sprint plans, the retros, and
# the layout design/evidence. Those explain decisions in this codebase and are
# cited by name from 20+ source and test files — c0-baseline.md alone from 13 —
# so gitignoring them left every one of those pointers dangling for anyone who
# cloned, and left the reasoning on a single laptop with no history.
#
# research/archive/ stays private: superseded planning INPUTS, and the market,
# persona and prioritisation work behind them. Not secret because it is
# embarrassing — it simply isn't anyone else's, and unlike the engineering
# record nothing in the codebase points at it.
research/archive/

# npm pack output — a local verification artifact, never committed
*.tgz

# Assembled landing-page tree — rebuilt by `npm run build:site`, never committed
_site/
